<article id="english" lang="en" aria-labelledby="en-title">
  <h2 id="en-title">LUMORA KINGDOM – Privacy Policy</h2>
  <p class="meta">Last updated: November 17, 2026 • Developer: TECNOLINE • Package: <code>com.tecnoline.lumorakingdom</code></p>
  <p>This policy explains game progress storage, advertising services, and privacy options in the LUMORA KINGDOM Android app. Third-party providers used by the app may also process information under their own privacy policies.</p>
  <h3>1. Game progress stored on your device</h3>
  <p>Level progress, stars, virtual currency, boosters, kingdom upgrades, rewards, and music/sound/other preferences are saved in the app's local storage. The current version does not offer player accounts or developer-operated cloud syncing, and this gameplay progress is not sent to TECNOLINE servers. Depending on your Android backup settings, app data may be included in device backups.</p>
  <h3>2. Advertising and third-party data</h3>
  <p>The app may display ads through Google AdMob (Google Mobile Ads SDK). Google and its advertising partners may process data such as IP addresses, inferred approximate location, device and app information, advertising identifiers where available, ad impressions and interactions, and diagnostics for ad delivery, measurement, security, fraud prevention, and personalization where allowed. The exact processing depends on your device settings, privacy choices, and Google's policies.</p>
  <p>Relevant links: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google AdMob information</a>.</p>
  <h3>3. Consent and privacy choices</h3>
  <p>Where required, a consent message may be shown through the Google User Messaging Platform (UMP). When available in your region, you can review or change your advertising privacy preferences from the game's Settings screen. You can also manage advertising-related choices through Android device privacy settings.</p>
  <h3>4. Permissions and game audio</h3>
  <p>The app uses internet and network-state access for advertising and consent management; advertising ID permission may be used on supported devices. Core gameplay does not request camera, microphone, contacts, or precise location permissions. Music and sound effects play from bundled app assets.</p>
  <h3>5. Children and age groups</h3>
  <p>The declared target audience, content rating, and ad settings are configured through Google Play Console. Any release directed at children must comply with applicable Google Play Families and advertising requirements.</p>
  <h3>6. Retention, deletion and requests</h3>
  <p>Gameplay data remains locally until the application is uninstalled or its storage is cleared. Clearing app data or uninstalling may remove saved progress; Android backups, if any, are managed through the relevant device and account settings. This version does not create a separate user account. Information processed by Google is subject to Google's retention and privacy controls. You can contact us with privacy requests using the email below.</p>
  <h3>7. Security and changes</h3>
  <p>Local gameplay data is kept in Android's app storage. Data transfer and security for third-party ad and consent services are managed by those providers. Updates to this policy will be published on this page.</p>
